{
  "id": "word-status-set-clear",
  "title": "setWordStatus and clearWordStatus: override set, set again, replaced, cleared, cleared again; derived statuses refused; entries without a note or a dictionary entry",
  "covers": [
    "words.status_set",
    "words.status_cleared",
    "words.status_clear_noop",
    "words.status_derived_refused",
    "words.status_no_note"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "Entry 1000220 has one note with a new meaning card; no override exists.",
    "Step 0: clearing when there is no override is 200 with the current status and mints nothing.",
    "Step 1 sets never_forget (override_origin manual). Step 2 sets the same status again: still 200 (the server emits again; the answer is the same status). Step 3 replaces it with blacklisted.",
    "Step 4: while the entry is blacklisted its card is not served (the queue is empty). Step 5 clears the override: the status is the derived one again. Step 6 clears again: the same status and updated_at, nothing minted. Step 7: the card is served again.",
    "Steps 8-9: new and learning are derived and cannot be set; an empty body is refused: 422 validation_failed.",
    "Step 10: an entry of the dictionary that has no note (1000440) takes an override; auto_status is null.",
    "Step 11: an entry that is in no dictionary (9999997) takes one too: the entry need not exist. The seq is in the path only, so it is listed in neither dict_entries nor dict_missing (those index entry_seq members and e:<seq> keys).",
    "Step 12: clearing an entry that has no row at all (1000450): 200, updated_at null."
  ],
